publisher body is not yet obtained. This is a source risk, not a novelty claim.

An author deduction predicts an exact all-target predecessor decoder by
directed cycles whose positive integer gaps sum to one circumference. It
implies bijectivity and entrance time zero when $M<n$. For $M\ge n$ no complete
